editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-08.md:107:"Was it forty-three?" Brom sounded only interested. "I lost the count. The whole of last year, the Ironyard and Greyvane together, I don't believe anybody got through to me forty-three times." He shifted the ice. "And nobody was out to hurt me. That's what I keep coming back to. Not one of the four wanted me hurt. They were all just right. Over and over again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-08.md-108-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-08.md-109-"You're Iron-equivalent," said Lira. She said it a little sharply, the way she said things she was going to defend. "Two years of circuit ratings. Greyvane's defensive cohort in a term."
