editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-32.md:39:He circled Brom at a walk, and then at a trot, and then at a walk, never still, round and round the fourth floor's grey boards. Brom had to turn to follow him, and every turn was a turn toward a door. Brom turned right, and that was nothing. Then the hill fighter changed direction without warning and Brom turned left after him, and in the middle of the turn, in the space of a breath while the guard went from one hand to the other, the hill fighter came in.
