editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-19.md-15-What the burst was for, the only thing it had ever been for, was being somewhere else when a blow arrived that somebody had meant. Somebody meant a blow, all the way, past the hinge where they could change their mind, and he went short off his hip and was not there when it arrived; and then they were in their recovery, going home, and he was out of the lock and into the gap. Every win he had on the slate that had a burst in it had been won like that.
