editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-20.md-127-His draw was Merrick: Shield Path, Copper Rank Four, fourteenth on the sheet, a fourth-year with a long face and a careful way of putting his feet down, as if every floor he stood on might have been laid by somebody who disliked him. He was no fool. Cael had a page on him, not a long one, but every line of it said the same thing in a different way: Merrick did not do what you expected, and he did not do what he wanted; he did what you could least afford.
