editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-20.md:129:And the whole cohort knew about Brom's seam. That was the thing Cael kept coming back to, on the east side of the tiers with the binder on his knee. It had been a private flaw once. Wray had found it at Greyvane with her own two hands, the gap in Brom's redirect between the read and the turn, and it had cost him nothing there, because nobody at Greyvane had been quick enough to get into it. Then Ephram had found it in three sessions on the east hall's timber, and spent a fortnight showing everyone else where it was. By now half the Copper column could have drawn it on a slate.
