editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-20.md-165-Merrick fed again, puzzled, and Brom took it again. A third time, and the third was not a feed at all but a real strike, full weight, to test whether the big man really meant it. He did. He took that one square too, on the forearm and into the shoulder, and Cael saw the guard come up a fraction slower afterward than it had before. He heard Brom's breathing go short and hard and rationed, like a man climbing a long hill at the end of a long day.
