editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-15.md-29-On the ninth, Cael did something he had not tried before. He did not reach harder. He chose a wider road. Before the force arrived he laid the line back out along Brom's arm and imagined it twice as broad, a channel cut for twice the water, and only then, when the push had settled fully into the bone, did he reach. The fragment gathered. It gathered further than it had ever gathered for him, a long, tightening pull that ran from his forearm up into his chest, and for a moment he held half of Brom's push in him like a breath he had taken too deep. Then he sent it home.
