    17	He took down everything in the press that so much as mentioned Iron Skin, which was three books. There was a big brown register of the Paths of the realm, a hundred years old and re-bound twice, and a smaller book on the defensive Paths in particular, and a guild almanac from a city up the coast with a chapter on the families who trained them. He carried all three to the table nearest the stove and sat with them through the whole of the cold afternoon.
