books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-35-
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:36:**The campus:** A former guild waystation complex on a hill town three days east of Ardenmere, converted to an academy sixty years ago. Minor-tier: one training hall that would fit inside a corner of a major academy's grounds, a lecture wing, a residence wing, an archive that predates the academy itself (the waystation's records room, never emptied), and a walled training yard. Greyvane's entire identity is that it takes students the tier system has mispriced — late Kindlers, disputed classifications, re-certification cases. It survives on being right about people other institutions were wrong about.
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-37-
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-38-**Key institutional facts:**
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-39-- *Provost Naveth:* Runs Greyvane. 60s, formerly a mid-tier academy administrator who took the Greyvane post as a demotion and made it a philosophy. Cautious by temperament, principled by conviction — the tension between those two is his whole arc this book. He approved Quenna's recruitment of Cael knowing it was legally fragile.
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-40-- *Quenna:* Carried over from Book 2 (LOCKED — see State Ledger). Senior teaching-practitioner, Silver-tier, irregular-Path development assessment. She administers the demonstration-provision track and is Cael's assessor of record. Her professional reputation is staked on this working.
