books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-94-The first weeks, structured around the divergence. For the first time since Book 1, the three of them are not living inside the same institution on the same terms — they're living inside the same institution on three *different* terms, and the chapter lets that reshape the daily texture.
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-95-
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-96-Brom disappears into standard coursework and comes back talkative — a word never previously applicable to Brom — about formal declaration theory, which he has spent his whole life deriving from scratch and is now being handed in organized form. His verdict: "Half of it is wrong. The wrong half is the half about ceilings." Filed, lightly, against his long arc.
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-97-
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:98:Lira's re-certification track is harder than advertised. The provision grants academic access but marks her file at every turn — separate sign-in on the training floor, an assessor's initial required beside her bout results. The academy is not cruel about it; the *procedure* is cruel on its own, without needing anyone's help. The chapter gives her one scene alone with the notice board, looking at her name with the provisional marker beside it, and one scene refusing to let it matter: she takes the floor against Greyvane's second-ranked student and wins with the not-holding-back circuit style that no academy taught her. The floor goes quiet. Fenmark's records say Copper-tier. The floor just watched something else.
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-99-
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-100-Cael's observer status is the strangest of the three: he may attend any lecture, use the library and archive, and train — but only under assessor supervision, only in scheduled sessions, never in open student bouts. He is present everywhere and eligible nowhere. He does what he does with every constraint: inventories it, finds its edges, and begins quietly filling twenty-three pages of the observation notebook with the declaration architecture of every Path on the training floor — more Path variety in two weeks than the circuit showed him in a year.
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-101-
books/book-03-no-path-given/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md-102-*Close on:* the Power Log, new entry: "Greyvane inventory, week two: eleven Paths I've never seen at close range. The observer category was meant as a cage. It's a vantage point."
--
