editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-22-- **Ilsev's six minutes**: the returns read verbatim at dictation speed [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: the edition's own texts: the first return as in B4 ch49:17–19, the second per B5 §10 item 17 [B5-reconciled 2026-10-06: confirmed verbatim, B5 ch58:21; audit §F D11], and Ilsev's standing note *Authorizing office: not traced.* (B4 ch46:147); not the source's compression; audit A10]; "The evaluation seat notes the contradiction…"; Karis's transcript and her one sentence. **Havel's window** (~2k): the minute carried to the copyists; the transfer request; six entries, done.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:23:- **The ruling**, read in two minutes forty: lawful, compliant, revoked; five weeks; chapter fourteen; *Given under the Compact's hand.* Withrow: "you did not lose badly"; Seln reads the hand; Brom squares the copy-sets by weight while Lira watches from the stair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-24-- **What Leaving Costs**: three roads priced; the cache argued for and lost out loud; **Bracken brings Brom's finding at night** — Iron, found, and the guidance note — "How many boxes is your research?" / "Three." / "Then I'm carrying three boxes."; Lira's whole bill; Karis's forfeiture priced in bibliography order (the Greyvane request redirected to Hesk; the assistant's letter); Seln's one sentence; **Ephram brought in, told the departure and nothing of the cache, asks for one bout**; five hands, Seln's last. **Withrow** alone: the four days she knew and said nothing; the other column; **"The record will say you left…"**; she opens the door herself. **Lira's window** (~1.5k) that night.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-25-- **The Last Bout** (~4,500–5,000): Rooke chalks it in the dark; the bluff and the town come; the Crown yard counted one last time; Ephram takes the sunward mark; the threes and the short beat; **the band refused — the lid comes off** [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: the Norhold rates and past them, shown on the bluff for the first time; audit A3] ("There it is. Three years. Again." [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: replaces "Two years"; Cael has been on the bluff since B4's start, so nearly three years; or no count; audit B7]); no flag; the reach in earnest, its price written the night before; the commitment engine turned; two touches to one [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: replaces "two flags to one"; the Crown-yard format is stated once, as two touches or as Rooke's own trial rule (OWNER #39); audit B2]; **the Blade notice**; Rooke's "Both. Enter both."; Gault's nod; Withrow last out; Lira's sentence; the boards ritual and **"Still glad."**; not told — the covenant's cost entered; the first pull (a lintel's edge); Anchor left in the kit and why; the empty yard: **"Good room."**
