editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:396:He had been seventeen for a year. It had been a long one. He had been seventeen at Norhold on the stone with a healer's fingers in his hand, and seventeen on the road home in a cart, and seventeen behind a bell-frame on a gatehouse roof, and seventeen five days ago on his knees in a chalk cut with a cage of points round him. And now he was not. Nothing in him had changed in the night. Nothing ever did, on a birthday. It was only a line in somebody's register moving down a row, but it was his line, and it had moved, and Lira had said it out loud across a refectory table before anybody else could.
